<title>JAPAN: Japan will act against excessive forex moves - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan will act against excessive forex moves - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Wednesday that Japan would act against any excessive movements in the currency market.  </p>
<p>Mitsuzuka told a parliamentary finance committee that both an excessively weak or strong yen is unfavourable for the economy.</p>
<p>&quot;It's good to have stable currencies,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Japan will take proper measures if currency moves are too rapid,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The dollar rose to 122.75 yen in Tokyo on Wednesday, its highest level in nearly four years.</p>
</text>
